Theorem TF-4: Project transfer produces Borrowed inheritance + borrow_sources entry

  Preconditions:
    - Instruction is `Project { value, field }` per Annex E §AIMS TF-4
    - `value` has AimsState `src.state` in the per-function state map
    - Per Appendix A row 5: `dst := (Borrowed, Linear, Once, src.uniq,
      src.loc, NonReusable, NONE)` — Uniqueness and Locality inherit from
      source; other 5 dimensions are constants per the table row
    - `borrow_sources` side-table populated per Annex E §AIMS — every
      Project creates exactly one entry tracking root + field-path

  Soundness property:
    Forall src in AimsState (non-SCALAR).
      transfer_tf4(Project { value: v, field: f }) where state(v) = src
      yields dst with:
        access := Borrowed; consumption := Linear; cardinality := Once;
        uniqueness := src.uniqueness; locality := src.locality;
        shape := NonReusable; effect := NONE = 0b000
    AND borrow_sources[dst] = { source: root(v), path: [field_chain] }
    AND L-6 layer (b) monotonicity: forall src1, src2. src1 ≤ src2 ⟹
      transfer_tf4(src1, f) ≤ transfer_tf4(src2, f) on the product order.

  Proof obligation:
    Three-part discharge:
      (a) Per-dimension output enumeration over (Uniqueness x Locality)
          source pairs — verify the 5 constant columns + 2 inherited columns
          match Appendix A row 5 for every (src.uniq, src.loc) pair.
      (b) borrow_sources side-table invariant per §1.9: every Project creates
          exactly ONE entry; no other instruction creates entries.
      (c) L-6 layer (b) monotonicity — Access/Consumption/Cardinality/Shape/
          Effect are constants (trivially monotone); Uniqueness and Locality
          inherit identity-style from source, which is monotone on its own
          carrier (identity on a totally-ordered chain is monotone by L-4).

    Part (a) — (Uniqueness x Locality) enumeration (3 x 5 = 15 pairs per
    Annex E §AIMS + §1.5 carriers):
      Uniqueness in {Unique, MaybeShared, Shared} (3 values)
      Locality in {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal, ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping,
                  Unknown} (5 values)
      For each of 15 (uniq, loc) pairs, build src state with constant
      Access=Owned, Consumption=Linear, Cardinality=Once, Shape=ReusableStruct,
      Effect=0b001, varying Uniqueness and Locality. Verify TF-4 output:
        access = Borrowed (constant per row)
        consumption = Linear (constant per row)
        cardinality = Once (constant per row)
        uniqueness = src.uniqueness (inherited)
        locality = src.locality (inherited)
        shape = NonReusable (constant per row)
        effect = NONE = 0b000 (constant per row)
      Note: CN-6 (Wide-locality uniqueness ceiling) and CN-8 (Borrowed
      locality ceiling) may post-canonicalize the TF-4 output:
        - CN-8 clamps Borrowed + (ArgEscaping | HeapEscaping | Unknown) to
          FunctionLocal — fires AFTER TF-4 emits the borrowed state.
        - CN-6 may then demote Unique -> MaybeShared if locality ≥
          HeapEscaping (cannot fire after CN-8 clamp for Borrowed paths).
      TF-4 proof discharges the PRE-CANONICALIZATION output per Appendix A
      conventions; CN-6 + CN-8 interaction discharged separately in §03.

    Part (b) — borrow_sources invariant per §1.9:
      "Every Project creates exactly one entry; no other instruction creates
      entries; read-only after intraprocedural analysis."
      Discharge: enumerate ArcInstr/ArcTerminator variants creating entries
      (count = 1: Project only) vs all other variants (count = 0).
      Engine verifies count = 1 for Project, exhaustive coverage absent for
      other variants in this proof's scope (cross-rule disjointness ships
      as composition theorem in §04.4).

    Part (c) — monotonicity per dimension:
      Access/Consumption/Cardinality/Shape/Effect: TF-4 emits constants
        (Borrowed, Linear, Once, NonReusable, 0b000). Constant function
        is monotone (Part (b) of TF-1 / TF-2a argument).
      Uniqueness: dst.uniqueness = src.uniqueness — identity on a totally-
        ordered 3-element chain {Unique, MaybeShared, Shared}. Identity
        on a chain is monotone trivially: u1 ≤ u2 ⟹ id(u1) ≤ id(u2).
      Locality: dst.locality = src.locality — identity on a 5-element chain
        {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal, ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping, Unknown}.
        Identity is monotone by the same argument.
      Per the componentwise-lift lemma (per L-1.proof Lift to product):
        if every per-dimension transfer is monotone, the product transfer
        is monotone.
      Representative monotonicity-pair enumeration discharged on 2 sample
      pairs spanning Uniqueness chain (Unique ≤ MaybeShared ≤ Shared) +
      Locality chain (BlockLocal ≤ FunctionLocal ≤ HeapEscaping).

    Engines dispatched:
      monotonicity (PRIMARY — L-6 layer (b) per-rule discharge per
        section_04::verify_tf4_project_borrowed_inherit — per-dimension
        monotone inheritance + product-lattice lift)
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — Appendix A row 5 enumeration across the
        3 x 5 (Uniqueness, Locality) source pair grid + §1.9 borrow_sources
        invariant check per section_04::verify_tf4_project_borrowed_inherit)
      lattice (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; product order at §02)
      refinement (SECONDARY — accepts gracefully; TF-4 does NOT refine())

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_04 monotonicity + case_analysis engines discharge TF-4 via 15-state (Uniqueness x Locality) enumeration + §1.9 borrow_sources singleton invariant + per-dimension constant/identity monotonicity
